#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md:6
msgid "Exercise: Generalized Operations"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md:8
msgid ""
"In the earlier pattern matching exercise, you created a `define_op!` macro "
"that defined a single binary operation for `i32` at a time."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md:11
msgid ""
"In this exercise, you will generalize that concept into a `define_ops!` "
"macro using the repetition constructs of macro matchers. The new macro "
"should allow implementing an arbitrary number of `std::ops` traits for a "
"generic wrapper type across multiple underlying numeric types in a single "
"macro invocation."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md:16
msgid "The desired macro syntax is:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md:27
msgid ""
"This invocation should implement `std::ops::Add`, `std::ops::Sub`, and "
"`std::ops::Mul` for `Scalar<i32>`, `Scalar<f32>`, and `Scalar<f64>`."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md:30
msgid "Instructions:"
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md:32
msgid ""
"Given a wrapper struct `#[derive(Debug, PartialEq)] struct Scalar<T>(pub "
"T);`, implement the `define_ops!` macro."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md:34
msgid ""
"Parse a comma-separated list of types (`$( $t:ty ),+`) followed by a colon "
"(`:`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md:36
msgid ""
"Parse a comma-separated list of trait mappings (`$( $trait_name:ident :: "
"$fn_name:ident => $op:tt ),*`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md:38
msgid ""
"In the macro expansion, use nested repetition `$($( ... )*)*` to generate "
"`impl std::ops::$trait_name for Scalar<$t>` blocks."
msgstr ""

#: src/macros/macro_rules/repetition/exercise.md:46
msgid "// TODO: Implement the `define_ops!` macro.\n"
msgstr ""

